# Configure Elasticsearch for local development

This guide helps you start a local Elasticsearch instance for development and testing.

## Before you begin

- You need Docker installed on your machine.
- You need permission to run local containers.
- You should be familiar with basic command-line usage.

## Start Elasticsearch

1. Create a Docker network for your local environment.
2. Start the Elasticsearch container with the required environment variables.
3. Verify that the cluster is healthy.

```bash
docker network create elastic

docker run -d --name es01 --network elastic -p 9200:9200 -p 9300:9300 \
  -e "discovery.type=single-node" \
  -e "xpack.security.enabled=false" \
  docker.elastic.co/elasticsearch/elasticsearch:8.15.0
```

4. Check the health endpoint.

```bash
curl -X GET "http://localhost:9200/_cluster/health?pretty"
```

